{"totalItems":1376,"success":true,"errors":[],"results":[{"productId":158276,"name":"World Championship Deck: 1997 Seattle - Jakub Slemr, World Champion","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 1997 Seattle Jakub Slemr World Champion","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158276_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158276/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-1997-seattle-jakub-slemr-world-champion","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:34:12.1","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Slemr's deck features a horde of fast, black creatures. Strengthening the speed kill are a variety of spells from all five colors.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158277,"name":"World Championship Deck: 1997 Seattle - Janosch Kuhn, Finalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 1997 Seattle Janosch Kuhn Finalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158277_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158277/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-1997-seattle-janosch-kuhn-finalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:34:18.703","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Kuhn's red, white, and blue deck maintains a sharp balance between speed and control.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158278,"name":"World Championship Deck: 1997 Seattle - Svend Geertsen, Semifinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 1997 Seattle Svend Geertsen Semifinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158278_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158278/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-1997-seattle-svend-geertsen-semifinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:34:33.237","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Geertsen's extremely fast monocolored deck is loaded with an army of green creatures. Giant Growth, Bounty of the Hunt, and Winter Orb provide the only noncreature power.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158279,"name":"World Championship Deck: 1997 Seattle - Paul McCabe, Semifinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 1997 Seattle Paul McCabe Semifinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158279_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158279/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-1997-seattle-paul-mccabe-semifinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:34:26.503","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"McCabe's fast red-blue deck puts the opponent on the defensive. A large number of inexpensive, efficient creatures overwhelm the opposition.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158280,"name":"World Championship Deck: 1998 Seattle - Brian Selden, World Champion","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 1998 Seattle Brian Selden World Champion","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158280_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158280/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-1998-seattle-brian-selden-world-champion","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:35:24.193","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"World Champion Brian Selden's deck conquered the field by using Survival of the Fittest to put creatures into the graveyard and Recurring Nightmare to bring them back into play. The deck employs more than twenty creatures and dips into blue for Lobotomy.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158281,"name":"World Championship Deck: 1998 Seattle - Ben Rubin, Finalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 1998 Seattle Ben Rubin Finalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158281_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158281/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-1998-seattle-ben-rubin-finalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:35:09.067","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Ben Rubin's archetypal red weenie deck took him all the way to the World Championship Finals. This aggressive Sligh deck consists of roughly equal parts direct damage, aggressive creatures, and land.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158282,"name":"World Championship Deck: 1998 Seattle - Brian Hacker, Quarterfinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 1998 Seattle Brian Hacker Quarterfinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158282_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158282/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-1998-seattle-brian-hacker-quarterfinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:35:16.487","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Brian Hacker's white weenie deck rolled over competitors with more than twenty aggressive creatures. This horde relies on creatures with shadow and the en-Kor to overwhelm the unprepared, with the threat of Cataclysm looming large.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158284,"name":"World Championship Deck: 1998 Seattle - Randy Buehler, Twelfth Place","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 1998 Seattle Randy Buehler Twelfth Place","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158284_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158284/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-1998-seattle-randy-buehler-twelfth-place","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:35:31.163","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Randy Buehler's Draw, Go deck is pure control, with over twenty counterspells and eight card-drawing engines to dig them out. The deck's offense is limited to Stalking Stones and a Rainbow Efreet, but the best offense is often a killer defense.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158285,"name":"World Championship Deck: 1999 Yokohama - Kai Budde, World Champion","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 1999 Yokohama Kai Budde World Champion","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158285_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158285/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-1999-yokohama-kai-budde-world-champion","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:36:02.55","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"World Champion Kai Budde's red-artifact deck employed more than 30 artifacts to generate huge amounts of mana. Big creatures like Masticore or Covetous Dragon became a threat to any opponent, and a well-timed Wildfire added the finishing touch.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158286,"name":"World Championship Deck: 1999 Yokohama - Mark Le Pine, Finalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 1999 Yokohama Mark Le Pine Finalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158286_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158286/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-1999-yokohama-mark-le-pine-finalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:36:18.907","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Mark Le Pine's aggressive 'Sped Red' deck applied the pressure early with 11 fast creatures before shifting into land-destruction mode. A late-game Cursed Scroll and Hammer of Bogardan would finish off his mana-crippled opponents.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158287,"name":"World Championship Deck: 1999 Yokohama - Matt Linde, Semifinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 1999 Yokohama Matt Linde Semifinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158287_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158287/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-1999-yokohama-matt-linde-semifinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:36:26.927","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Matt Linde's speedy mono-green deck contained 26 low-cost creatures. Supplementing this nasty creature assault were four Rancors and four Giant Growths. If his opponent wasn't smothered by furn five, Linde's Cursed Scrolls would pick up the slack.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158288,"name":"World Championship Deck: 1999 Yokohama - Jakub Slemr, Quarterfinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 1999 Yokohama Jakub Slemr Quarterfinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158288_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158288/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-1999-yokohama-jakub-slemr-quarterfinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:35:54.847","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Jakub Slemr's mono-black deck controlled the board with Cursed Scrolls, Powder Kegs, and Phrexian Plaguelords. His 'Black Control' creation also pounded his opponents early with discard effects found in Ravenous Rats, Duress, and Stupor.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158290,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2000 Brussels - Jon Finkel, World Champion","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2000 Brussels Jon Finkel World Champion","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158290_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158290/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2000-brussels-jon-finkel-world-champion","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:36:55.99","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Jon Finkel's explosive, mono-blue deck used artifacts such as Grim Monolith, Metalworker, and Voltaic Key to generate huge amounts of mana. The mana, in turn, put large creatures into play to finish off stunned opponents.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158291,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2000 Brussels - Janosch Kuhn, Quarterfinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2000 Brussels Janosch Kuhn Quarterfinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158291_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158291/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2000-brussels-janosch-kuhn-quarterfinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:36:49.247","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Janosch Kuhn's red-green deck used Birds of Paradise and Llanowar Elves to build up mana early in the game. Kuhn then delivered the finishing punch with mana-denial cards, such as Stone Rain and Plow Under.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158292,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2000 Brussels - Tom van de Logt, Quarterfinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2000 Brussels Tom van de Logt Quarterfinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158292_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158292/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2000-brussels-tom-van-de-logt-quarterfinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:37:12.767","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Tom van de Logt's Replenish deck uses cards like Attunement and Frantic Search to put powerful enchantments into the graveyard. Then he used Replenish to put all of the enchantments back into play at once and pound his opponents.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158293,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2000 Brussels - Nicolas Labarre, Quarterfinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2000 Brussels Nicolas Labarre Quarterfinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158293_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158293/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2000-brussels-nicolas-labarre-quarterfinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-07T13:37:05.607","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Nicolas Labarre's combo deck, called Chimera, used searching cards to fetch Fecundity, Saproling Cluster, and Ashnod's Alter so he could generate unlimited mana. With this mana Labarre used Blaze or Whetstone to plow right over his opponents.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158294,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2001 Toronto - Tom van de Logt, World Champion","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2001 Toronto Tom van de Logt World Champion","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158294_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158294/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2001-toronto-tom-van-de-logt-world-champion","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T15:05:17.79","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Tom van de Logt's aggressive, black-red 'Machine Head' deck used the good ol' 'blow stuff up' method. While creatures like Plague Spitter wiped out his opponents' smaller creatures, more ferocious beasts like Flametongue Kavu aggressively cleared the board of larger threats.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158296,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2001 Toronto - Alex Borteh, Finalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2001 Toronto Alex Borteh Finalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158296_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158296/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2001-toronto-alex-borteh-finalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T15:04:48.16","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Alex Borteh's monoblue combo deck contained twelve 1-toughness creatures. These helped hold the board until his Static Orb-Opposition combo could lock down his opponents' permanents--clearing the way for a horde of Merfolk to pour through for the victory.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158297,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2001 Toronto - Antoine Ruel, Semifinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2001 Toronto Antoine Ruel Semifinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158297_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158297/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2001-toronto-antoine-ruel-semifinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T15:04:54.98","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Antoine Ruel's blue-black-red control deck survived the pressure in the early game with its almost overwhelming card-drawing capability. And in the end, Nether Spirit kept rising from his graveyard to take down his opponents.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158298,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2001 Toronto - Jan Tomcani, Quarterfinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2001 Toronto Jan Tomcani Quarterfinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158298_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158298/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2001-toronto-jan-tomcani-quarterfinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T15:05:07.287","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Jan Tomcani's green-red-black 'Fires\"' deck used early mana-producing creatures to play a quick Fires of Yavimaya. Shortly thereafter, Tomcani's hasted big creatures pounded opponents' life totals to dust.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158300,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2002 Sydney - Carlos Romao, World Champion","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2002 Sydney Carlos Romao World Champion","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158300_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158300/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2002-sydney-carlos-romao-world-champion","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T15:05:44.117","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Romao's blue-black 'Psychatog' deck was the defining deck of the tournament. A control deck at heart, with lots of card drawing and countermagic, it wants to stall an opponent until it can play a devastating Upheaval and Psychatog on the same turn. While many people at this year's World Championship played this style of deck, Carlos simply played his version better than everyone else played theirs.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158301,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2002 Sydney - Sim Han How, Quarterfinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2002 Sydney Sim Han How Quarterfinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158301_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158301/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2002-sydney-sim-han-how-quarterfinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T15:06:08.01","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Han How's blue-green-red 'Squirrel Opposition' deck can be aggressive with cards like Wild Mongrel and Flametongue Kavu, or it can play the stalling game with a Squirrel Nest - Opposition combo. Beware the Roar of the Wurm in the sideboard!\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158302,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2002 Sydney - Brian Kibler, 11th Place","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2002 Sydney Brian Kibler 11th Place","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158302_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158302/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2002-sydney-brian-kibler-11th-place","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T15:05:33.33","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Kibler's green-white-red 'Red Zone 2K2' deck loves to put creatures into the 'Red Zone'; that is, attack with them! This aggressive deck can put over thirty creatures on the board. And with Glory in the graveyard, few defenses can prevail against their onslaught.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158303,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2002 Sydney - Raphael Levy, 16th Place","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2002 Sydney Raphael Levy 16th Place","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158303_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158303/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2002-sydney-raphael-levy-16th-place","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T15:05:54.367","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Levy's blue-green 'Le Wonder Goose' deck features a ton of small green creatures like Nimble Mongoose and Werebear. With Careful Study and Mental Note to get to threshold, however, those small creatures quickly turn into real monsters!\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158305,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2003 Berlin - Daniel Zink, World Champion","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2003 Berlin Daniel Zink World Champion","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158305_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158305/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2003-berlin-daniel-zink-world-champion","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T14:54:24.303","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Daniel Zink's white-blue-green 'Wake' deck is a control deck at heart. Once the powerful enchantment Mirari's Wake is in play, the deck produces more mana, draws more cards, counters more spells, and makes more Soldiers than opponents can possibly handle.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158306,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2003 Berlin - Dave Humpherys, Semifinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2003 Berlin Dave Humpherys Semifinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158306_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158306/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2003-berlin-dave-humpherys-semifinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T14:54:15.097","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Dave 'The Hump' Humpherys' blue-green deck combines the many madness cards from the Torment set, including Basking Rootwalla, Arrogant Wurm, and Circular Logic, with discard-enablers like Aquamoeba and Wild Mongrel for tremendous effect.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158308,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2003 Berlin - Wolfgang Eder, Quarterfinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2003 Berlin Wolfgang Eder Quarterfinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158308_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158308/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2003-berlin-wolfgang-eder-quarterfinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T14:56:37.66","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Wolfgang Eder introduced the black-red 'Goblin Bidding' deck to the world at the European Championships. The typical Goblin hoard deck gets an incredible midgame play in Patriarch's Bidding, which brings every Goblin in the graveyard back in to play.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158309,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2003 Berlin - Peer Kroger, Quarterfinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2003 Berlin Peer Kroger Quarterfinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158309_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158309/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2003-berlin-peer-kroger-quarterfinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T14:56:33.9","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Hometown hero Peer Kröger's 'Reanimator' deck was a nightmare for his opponents! This black-red deck excels at putting scary monsters into the graveyard and then bringing them into play.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158310,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2004 San Francisco - Julien Nuijten, World Champion","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2004 San Francisco Julien Nuijten World Champion","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158310_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158310/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2004-san-francisco-julien-nuijten-world-champion","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T14:45:13.947","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"The youngest ever Magic World Champion, Dutch wunderkind Julien Nujiten came out of nowhere to stun the field. Just fifteen years old, Nujiten proved that he can play with the best. Playing a green-white Astral Slide deck designed to destroy 'Affinity', he posted a respectable 4-2 record on the Standard day at Worlds and then calmly swept the field on the final day. He says the inspiration for his deck came from an Internet article by Pro Tour veteran Brian Kibler.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158311,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2004 San Francisco - Aeo Paquette, Finalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2004 San Francisco Aeo Paquette Finalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158311_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158311/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2004-san-francisco-aeo-paquette-finalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T14:46:59.94","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Professional Magic player Aeo Paquette played the deck that defined the metagame at the 2004 World Championships: 'Affinity.' Against a field full of decks designed to beat Affinity, this nineteen-year-old Canadian piloted his deck to a 5-1 record during the Standard portion of the tournament. Paquette credits his friend Jeff Cunningham for helping him design an Affinity deck that could compete so well against the field.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158312,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2004 San Francisco - Manuel Bevand, Semifinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2004 San Francisco Manuel Bevand Semifinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158312_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158312/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2004-san-francisco-manuel-bevand-semifinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T14:45:04.423","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Pro Tour veteran Manuel Bevand played an artifact-based combo deck to a perfect 6-0 record on the Standard day at Worlds. His deck uses Krark-Clan Ironworks to quickly get a Myr Incubator into play, which then creates thirty or more 1/1 creatures -- sometimes as early as the third turn! A twenty-seven-year-old freelance game designer from Paris, France, Bevand has been a Magic regular since 1994, playing in over a dozen Pro Tour events. He credits Magic Online for getting him back into championship form.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158313,"name":"World Championship Deck: 2004 San Francisco - Gabriel Nassif, Quarterfinalist","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 2004 San Francisco Gabriel Nassif Quarterfinalist","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158313_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158313/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-2004-san-francisco-gabriel-nassif-quarterfinalist","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T14:46:52.36","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<em>\"Twenty-year-old Gabriel Nassif is considered to be the best player never to have won a Pro Tour event. Designed to beat the ubiquitous 'Affinity' decks, his blue-white control deck also plays well against anti-Affinity decks. Worlds marked the third time in the season that the Parisian had made it to the final day of a Pro Tour event, and his performance earned Nassif the coveted 2004 Player of the Year award -- a title he will defend vigorously next year.\"</em>\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158314,"name":"World Championship Deck: 1996 New York City - Mark Justice","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 1996 New York City Mark Justice","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158314_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158314/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-1996-new-york-city-mark-justice","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T13:27:41.767","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<strong>NOTE: The cards in this deck are gold-bordered with an alternate card backing and are printed with the player's signature. They are NOT tournament legal.</strong>"}]},{"productId":158315,"name":"World Championship Deck: 1996 New York City - Bertrand Lestree","cleanName":"World Championship Deck 1996 New York City Bertrand Lestree","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/158315_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/158315/magic-world-championship-decks-world-championship-deck-1996-new-york-city-bertrand-lestree","modifiedOn":"2018-02-06T13:32:14.42","imageCount":1,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"release