"productId":164272,"name":"Wrath of God - 2000 Tom van de Logt (6ED)","cleanName":"Wrath of God 2000 Tom van de Logt 6ED","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/164272_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/164272/magic-world-championship-decks-wrath-of-god-2000-tom-van-de-logt-6ed","modifiedOn":"2018-04-04T18:11:06.86","imageCount":2,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"Rarity","displayName":"Rarity","value":"S"},{"name":"SubType","displayName":"Creature Type or Sub Type","value":"Sorcery"},{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"Destroy all creatures. They can't be regenerated.\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>Not a Tournament Legal card.</strong>"}]},{"productId":164273,"name":"2000 Tom van de Logt Biography Card","cleanName":"2000 Tom van de Logt Biography Card","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/164273_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/164273/magic-world-championship-decks-2000-tom-van-de-logt-biography-card","modifiedOn":"2018-04-04T18:14:00.56","imageCount":2,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"Rarity","displayName":"Rarity","value":"S"},{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"(Quarterfinalist)\r\n<br>\r\n<br>Quarterfinalist Tom van de Logt posted a perfect 6-0 record during the standard portion of this year's World Championships. The 19-year-old Groesbeek, Holland native was playing a deck that had a big impact on the metagame this year, \"Replenish\". This deck used cards like Attunement and Frantic Search to put powerful enchantments, such as Parallax Wave and Opalescence, into the graveyard and then used Replensh to put them all back into play at once."}]},{"productId":164274,"name":"2000 Tom van de Logt Decklist Card","cleanName":"2000 Tom van de Logt Decklist Card","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/164274_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/164274/magic-world-championship-decks-2000-tom-van-de-logt-decklist-card","modifiedOn":"2018-04-04T18:14:42.013","imageCount":2,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"Rarity","displayName":"Rarity","value":"S"}]},{"productId":164307,"name":"2001 Tom van de Logt Biography Card","cleanName":"2001 Tom van de Logt Biography Card","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/164307_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/164307/magic-world-championship-decks-2001-tom-van-de-logt-biography-card","modifiedOn":"2019-05-09T17:26:37.99","imageCount":2,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"Rarity","displayName":"Rarity","value":"S"},{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"(World Champion)\r\n<br>\r\n<br>Tom van de Logt is the 2001 Netherlands National Champion as well as one of an elite group of players who have posted back-to-back World Championship Top 8 performances. Currently a student in Groesbeek, van de Logt posted an impressive 5-1 record in the Standard portion of this year's Worlds. He described his aggressive black-red \"Machine Head\" deck as \"the deck that beats the deck that beats 'fires.'\" He liked the explosive \"I win\" draws that his deck provided, and he especially liked the way it performed against blue decks."}]},{"productId":164308,"name":"2001 Tom van de Logt Decklist Card","cleanName":"2001 Tom van de Logt Decklist Card","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/164308_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/164308/magic-world-championship-decks-2001-tom-van-de-logt-decklist-card","modifiedOn":"2018-04-06T12:16:38.79","imageCount":2,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"Rarity","displayName":"Rarity","value":"S"}]},{"productId":164309,"name":"2001 World Championship Blank Card","cleanName":"2001 World Championship Blank Card","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/164309_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/164309/magic-world-championship-decks-2001-world-championship-blank-card","modifiedOn":"2018-04-06T12:18:06.683","imageCount":2,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"Rarity","displayName":"Rarity","value":"S"}]},{"productId":164310,"name":"2001 World Championship Advertisement Card","cleanName":"2001 World Championship Advertisement Card","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/164310_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/164310/magic-world-championship-decks-2001-world-championship-advertisement-card","modifiedOn":"2024-08-20T18:21:26.81","imageCount":2,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"Rarity","displayName":"Rarity","value":"S"},{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<strong>Collect All Four World Championship Decks</strong>\r\n<br>Relive the excitement of the 2001 World Championships with these four commemorative decks.\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>Tom van de Logt, World Champion—</strong>Tom van de Logt's aggressive, black-red \"Machine Head\" deck used the good ol' \"blow stuff up\" method. While creatures like Plague Spitter wiped out his opponent's smaller creatures, more ferocious beasts like Flametongue Kavu aggressively cleared the board of larger threats.\r\n<br><strong>Alex Borteh, Finalist—</strong>Alex Borteh's monoblue combo deck contained twelve 1-toughness creatures. These helped hold the board until his Static Orb—Opposition combo could lock down his opponents' permanents—clearing the way for a horde of Merfolk that pour through for the victory.\r\n<br><strong>Antoine Ruel, Semifinalist—</strong>Antoine Ruel's blue-black-red control deck survived the pressure in the early game with its almost overwhelming card-drawing capability. And in the end, Nether Spirit kept rising from his graveyard to take down his opponents.\r\n<br><strong>Jan Tomcani, Quarterfinalist—</strong>Jan Tomcani's green-red-black \"Fires\" deck used early mono-producing creatures to play a quick Fires of Yavimaya. Shortly thereafter, Tomcani's hasted big creatures pounded opponents' life totals to dust."}]},{"productId":164311,"name":"Addle - 2001 Tom van de Logt (INV) (SB)","cleanName":"Addle 2001 Tom van de Logt INV SB","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/164311_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/164311/magic-world-championship-decks-addle-2001-tom-van-de-logt-inv-sb","modifiedOn":"2018-04-06T12:40:58.777","imageCount":2,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"Rarity","displayName":"Rarity","value":"S"},{"name":"SubType","displayName":"Creature Type or Sub Type","value":"Sorcery"},{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"Choose a color. Look at target player's hand and choose a card of that color from it. That player discards that card.\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>Not a Tournament Legal card.</strong>\r\n<br><em>”SB” indicates this is a sideboard card.</em>"},{"name":"FlavorText","displayName":"Flavor","value":"<em>\"I'll wring out your tiny mind like a sponge.\" —Urborg witch</em>"}]},{"productId":164312,"name":"Blazing Specter - 2001 Tom van de Logt (INV)","cleanName":"Blazing Specter 2001 Tom van de Logt INV","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/164312_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/164312/magic-world-championship-decks-blazing-specter-2001-tom-van-de-logt-inv","modifiedOn":"2018-04-06T12:46:59.35","imageCount":2,"presaleInfo":{"isPre