presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"Rarity","displayName":"Rarity","value":"S"},{"name":"SubType","displayName":"Creature Type or Sub Type","value":"Instant"},{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<strong>Wax</strong> (G)\r\n<br>Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>Wane</strong> (W)\r\n<br>Destroy target enchantment. \r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>Not a Tournament Legal card.</strong>"}]},{"productId":173483,"name":"Wild Mongrel - 2002 Brian Kibler (ODY)","cleanName":"Wild Mongrel 2002 Brian Kibler ODY","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/173483_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/173483/magic-world-championship-decks-wild-mongrel-2002-brian-kibler-ody","modifiedOn":"2018-08-06T19:08:02.053","imageCount":2,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"Rarity","displayName":"Rarity","value":"S"},{"name":"SubType","displayName":"Creature Type or Sub Type","value":"Creature — Hound"},{"name":"P","displayName":"P","value":"2"},{"name":"T","displayName":"T","value":"2"},{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"Discard a card from your hand: Wild Mongrel gets +1/+1 and becomes the color of your choice until end of turn.\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>Not a Tournament Legal card.</strong>"},{"name":"FlavorText","displayName":"Flavor","value":"<em>It teaches</em> you<em> to play dead.</em>"}]},{"productId":173484,"name":"2002 World Championship Blank Card","cleanName":"2002 World Championship Blank Card","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/173484_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/173484/magic-world-championship-decks-2002-world-championship-blank-card","modifiedOn":"2018-08-06T19:11:40.577","imageCount":2,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"Rarity","displayName":"Rarity","value":"S"}]},{"productId":173485,"name":"2002 World Championship Advertisement Card","cleanName":"2002 World Championship Advertisement Card","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/173485_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/173485/magic-world-championship-decks-2002-world-championship-advertisement-card","modifiedOn":"2019-02-04T17:01:39.043","imageCount":2,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"Rarity","displayName":"Rarity","value":"S"},{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"<strong>Collect All Four World Championship Decks</strong>\r\n<br>Relive the excitement of the 2001 World Championships with these four commemorative decks.\r\n<br>\r\n<br><strong>Carlos Romao, World Champion—</strong>Romao's blue-black \"Psychatog\" deck was the defining deck of the tournament. A control deck at heart, with lots of card drawing and countermagic, it wants to stall an opponent until it can play a devastating Upheaval and Psychatog on the same turn.\r\n<br><strong>Sim Han How, Quarterfinalist—</strong>Han How's blue-green-red \"Squirrel Obsession\" deck can be aggressive with cards like Wild Mongrel and Flametongue Kavu, or it can be the stalling game with a Squirrel Nest—Opposition combo. Beware the Roare of the Wurms in the sideboard!\r\n<br><strong>Brian Kibler, Eleventh Place—</strong>Kibler's green-white-red- \"Red Zone 2K2\" deck loves to put creatures into the \"red zone\"; that is, attack with them! This aggressive deck can put over thirty creatures on the board. And with Glory in the graveyard, few defenses can prevail against their onslaught.\r\n<br><strong>Raphael Levy, Sixteenth Place—</strong>Levy's blue-green \"Le Wonder Goose\" deck features a ton of small green creatures like Nimble Mongoose and Werebear. With Careful Study and Mental Note to get to threshold, however, those small creatures quickly turn into real monsters!"}]},{"productId":173486,"name":"2002 Carlos Romao Biography Card","cleanName":"2002 Carlos Romao Biography Card","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/173486_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/173486/magic-world-championship-decks-2002-carlos-romao-biography-card","modifiedOn":"2018-08-06T19:21:25.78","imageCount":2,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"Rarity","displayName":"Rarity","value":"S"},{"name":"OracleText","displayName":"Rules Text Contains","value":"(World Champion)\r\n<br>Carlos Romao played the same style of deck that many people at this year's World Championships chose to play: blue-black Psychatog. He simply played his version better than everyone else played theirs. Romao, known as \"Jaba\" to his friends, was a perfect 6-0 during the Swiss portion of the tournament, posting a stunning 12-0 game record. This twenty-year-old native of Sao Paulo, Brazil, has been widely regarded as one of the best players in South America. His deck tried to stay alive long enough to play Upheaval, while floating mana to replay Psychatog on the same turn."}]},{"productId":173487,"name":"2002 Carlos Romao Decklist Card","cleanName":"2002 Carlos Romao Decklist Card","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/173487_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.com/product/173487/magic-world-championship-decks-2002-carlos-romao-decklist-card","modifiedOn":"2018-08-06T19:21:59.317","imageCount":2,"presaleInfo":{"isPresale":false,"releasedOn":null,"note":null},"extendedData":[{"name":"Rarity","displayName":"Rarity","value":"S"}]},{"productId":173488,"name":"Cephalid Coliseum - 2002 Carlos Romao (ODY)","cleanName":"Cephalid Coliseum 2002 Carlos Romao ODY","imageUrl":"https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com/product/173488_200w.jpg","categoryId":1,"groupId":2198,"url":"https://www.tcgplayer.c